  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A uniform electric field <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mi>m</mi></mrow><mi>e</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> is created between two parallel plates of length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> as shown in figure, (where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo></math> mass of electron and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>e</mi><mo>=</mo></math> charge of electron). An electron enters the field symmetrically between the plates with a speed of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The angle of the deviation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>&theta;</mi></mfenced></math> of the path of the electron as it comes out of the field will be _____ .</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/842a1b33-c73e-45f6-bb43-e46c56c072fd-image.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 123px;\" /></p>",
